Haakon Studebaker <heptapod@gmail.com> wrote:
>Priests don't accept identified gems in lieu of gold for their various 
>benefits (that could be a YANI). In the end, they're just good for boosting 
>luck with unicorns and increasing one's score at the end of a long slog 
>through the Dungeons of Doom.

Gems are good for:
1. Boosting luck by throwing them to unicorns.
2. Increasing your score if you ascend. Of course, since your score is
   in fact completely meaningless if you've managed to ascend, using
   gems for this purpose provides negative benefit.
3. Selling to shopkeepers for money or credit. This is quite handy.

#1 and #3 are useful in the early game and usually useless in the late
game.  However, there are many items whose properties are useful in the
early game and usually useless in the late game, so that's OK :)
